MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings › AI showed each account as a chip ("Default · no space yet")
whose click only opened rename / Sign in… / Remove: the one place to
choose a space's account was the space's right-click menu, which
Settings didn't point to. Under each AI with two accounts or more,
Settings now has one picker per space ("Claude in Work: ~/.claude ▾"),
the same choice as the space's menu.

When the login environment points the CLI elsewhere
(CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude-personal), its own folder was labelled
"Default" next to the real default ("Personal (default)"); it is now
"~/.claude" until the person names it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
